The Amidah blessing for justice is called Hashiva Shofteinu (“Restore our judges”). It asks for the return of righteous leadership and fair judgment. Here is a clear English version:

Amidah – Prayer for Justice (Hashiva Shofteinu)

Restore our judges as in former times,
and our counselors as at the beginning.

Remove from us sorrow and sighing,
and reign over us, You alone,
with kindness and compassion,
and justify us in judgment.

Blessed are You, Lord,
the King who loves righteousness and justice.

================================================================================
Slightly expanded traditional-style translation:

Restore our judges as at first and our counselors as at the beginning;
remove from us grief and anguish;
and reign over us, You alone, O Lord,
with lovingkindness and compassion,
and make us righteous in judgment.

Blessed are You, Lord,
King who loves righteousness and justice.

This blessing expresses the hope for a just society rooted in fairness, compassion, and moral leadership.

